66,2,1,talk,Sakura,,Oh no! Midori is gone! That's so sad! Who could be so mean to do that? I'm actually a little bit scared now...,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,2,1,talk,Shion,,Midori was the peacemaker. Removing her ensures the group remains fragmented and easier to manipulate. This was a strategic kill.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"A calculated move. With Rin executed and Midori gone, the pool of suspects has shrunk. We must be even more precise now.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"Maybe the wolf is just really hungry! But we have to find them before they eat us too! @Shion, you're so smart, do you know who it is?","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Sakura, your constant playfulness is becoming a liability. You've avoided taking a firm stance on anyone's behavior since the start.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"I agree. Sakura's ""innocent"" persona is a convenient shield. It allows her to probe others without ever revealing her own logic.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,2,3,talk,Sakura,,Me?! But I'm just a little girl! I don't know how to be a scary wolf! I just want us all to be friends!,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,2,3,talk,Shion,,"The ""innocent"" act is the oldest trick in the book. You are the only one left whose speech patterns haven't shifted to match the situation.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,Precisely. The contrast between your levity and the current gravity of our situation is no longer charming; it is suspicious.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,2,4,talk,Sakura,,"You guys are being meanies! I'm not a wolf! I'm just Sakura! If you vote for me, you're making a big, big mistake!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,2,4,talk,Shion,,"A mistake is a result of missing data. We have the data: your deflection, your lack of substance, and the elimination of the others.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"The logic is sound. Between Shion and Sakura, the latter's behavior is entirely inconsistent with a Villager's goal of finding the enemy.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shion"",""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
